## 🧠 CORE DESIGN

### 1. Idempotent Job Creation (No Duplicates)
- Each request must generate a deduplication key:
    job_key = repo_id + job_type + commit_hash (or request_id)  
- Create jobs using atomic upsert
- Add unique index on job_key
- If duplicate request comes:
  - return existing job_id
  - DO NOT create new job

---

### 2. Atomic Job Claiming (THREAD-SAFE / PROCESS-SAFE)

Workers MUST claim jobs using MongoDB findOneAndUpdate ONLY:

Criteria:
- status = QUEUED OR RETRYABLE
- OR status = IN_PROGRESS AND lease_until expired

Atomic update:
- set status = IN_PROGRESS
- set leased_by = worker_id
- set lease_until = now + timeout
- increment attempts

⚠️ NEVER:
- use find() then update()
- use in-memory locks

This is the ONLY concurrency control.

---

### 3. Lease-Based Processing (Crash Safe)
- Every job has lease_until
- If worker crashes:
  - job becomes reclaimable after lease expiry
- Workers must:
  - process ONLY jobs they leased
  - verify lease ownership before updating status

---

### 4. Strict Manifest Validation (FAIL FAST)

Before processing:
- repo_id exists
- repo_path exists
- repo_path accessible

If invalid:
- mark job FAILED
- log exact reason
- DO NOT continue

---

### 5. Startup Health Check (FAIL FAST)

On app start:
- verify MongoDB connection
- verify collections exist
- verify indexes exist

If ANY fails:
- STOP application
- log CRITICAL error

No “best-effort” mode allowed.

